@* Tabs of the analysis section.

   Analysis and impact stood side by side as two equal menu items, and the
   names suggested they do the same thing. They do not: one is a report about
   what was, the other a tool for what would be.

   Merging them would mean pressing a tool into a report - the same category
   error that made "Why?" look wrong in the main menu. What connects them is
   the question behind both: what does the filtering do in this network? Once
   computed against what happened, once computed forward against what would.

   Hence one menu item, two tabs. Both addresses stay valid, so existing
   bookmarks keep working. *@

<nav class="subnav">
    <NavLink href="analytics" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">@T.TabHistory</NavLink>
    <NavLink href="impact">@T.TabRuleImpact</NavLink>
</nav>

@code {
    [Inject] private Auspex.Control.Services.Localization.Strings T { get; set; } = default!;
}
